    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d326-a3">

                <pb facs="0456" n="376" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg376"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Swenson to Dr.
                            Deuntzer</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Copenhagen</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-02-21"><hi rendition="#italic">February 21,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 142.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: Referring to my Nos. 139 and 140 of
                    January 28 and February 7, respectively, in the military service case of James
                    Nelson, I have the honor to inclose herewith a notice,<anchor n="a"
                        xml:id="d326-f1"/> a petition,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d326-f2"/> and a
                    transcript of the court records,<anchor n="a" xml:id="d326-f3"/> which Mr.
                    Nelson has forwarded to me through his attorney, C. B. Olivarius, of Nyköbing,
                    Falster, with the request that I submit the same to the proper authorities. Mr.
                    Nelson’s delicate health suffers from the nervous strain caused by the sense of
                    imprisonment, and I would earnestly repeat my request of the 7th instant that
                    his sentence be commuted.</p>
                <p>Be pleased, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Laurits S.
                    Swenson.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
